    "stars": 3,
    "text": "I rarely write reviews, but since this place has been so highly recommended by friends and strangers, I feel compelled to share my experience.\nWe started queing at 20:10 and waited in line for over two hours. Why? Not for the queue itsself but for the service. There were only two people working inside the shop, with little to no organization.\n\nMoreover, and this is the most depresssing part, the doner was overall mid: the ingredients you can choose are very few (the best one was the grated cheese), the sauces are mild and a bit tasteless (except for the spicy one, which was actually pretty good) and the meat is a classic, basic, chicken kebap. In conclusion, if this is your first time trying a kebap, you can find a much better one; if you are used to eating kebap… you also can find a better one.\n\nNota per i romani: se avete mai preso un kebab senza pretese a Roma, avete mangiato questo. La prossima volta che vi nominano Mustafa ricordategli Alibabà.",
    "textTranslated": null
  },
